From b7f2cf8cd1641a8cede22673ebcc51a600117e15 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:19:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] remote notice index: busy is not corrupt, holder
 backoff, gateway role upgrade

Follow-ups to PR #2177 (review 5890676663 nits; card t_01a1d4ceafdeb67c).

1. `_open_rw` caught every `sqlite3.DatabaseError`, which includes
   OperationalError 'database is locked', and unlinked the copy as corrupt.
   A mode=ro reader holding a read transaction on a not-yet-WAL index makes
   `PRAGMA journal_mode=WAL` raise locked, so a healthy copy was deleted and
   recreated. Now only SQLITE_CORRUPT / SQLITE_NOTADB (message fallback:
   'file is not a database', 'malformed') recreate it; busy/locked raises,
   `publish` counts it in `stats["busy"]` and returns False (readers compute
   locally, as on any miss).
2. `_hold` set `last` only when refresh returned True, so with no flock or a
   publish that keeps failing every process reran replica_key + compute +
   published_key every second. A failed (or raising) refresh now backs off,
   doubling from the poll interval to BACKOFF_MAX_S (60 s); success resets
   it and remembers the stamp. `ensure_holder` starts nothing when fcntl is
   None (publishing needs flock, so such a holder could never succeed).
3. The lease role was whichever `ensure_holder` call came first, so a
   gateway whose collect() ran before kanban_remote_owner._collect held the
   lease as 'serve'. `_holders` now records the role priority; a later
   higher-role claim stops the lower refresher and starts one under the new
   role. Call-site comments fixed.

Tests (tests/tui_gateway/test_kanban_remote_index.py):
- test_busy_index_is_skipped_not_deleted_as_corrupt (the repro above)
- test_holder_backs_off_while_publishing_fails (frozen injectable clock)
- test_no_holder_without_flock
- test_gateway_claim_upgrades_a_serve_holder

RED on the pre-fix base e9d537b75a (tests only): all 4 fail (publish returned
True after deleting the copy; no `_clock`; a holder spawned without fcntl;
the gateway claim spawned nothing). GREEN: 15/15 in the file; 535 tests in
the 36 files importing kanban_remote_{index,owner,notices} pass;
scripts/check --base origin/main ok.
